00AB   D9                     EXX      
00AC   CD 2B 00               CALL   jphl   
00AF   D9                     EXX      
00B0   2A 34 82               LD   HL,(RSAVE)   
00B3   D9                     EXX      
00B4   E1                     POP   HL   
00B5   F7                     RST   30h   
00B6                             ; ---- the letters and digits (here, in the middle, so that the inner loop's
00B6                             ; ---- short jumps reach them, and the handlers after them reach rpushn) ------
00B6                             ; Digits: step back onto the first digit and read the whole number.
00B6   E5           DIGIT:    PUSH   HL   
00B7   0B                     DEC   BC   
00B8   CD A8 02               CALL   rdnum   
00BB   F7                     RST   30h   
00BC                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
00BC   E5           LOWER:    PUSH   HL   
00BD   87                     ADD   A,A   
00BE   6F                     LD   L,A   
00BF   26 82                  LD   H,LETPAGE   
00C1   F7                     RST   30h   
00C2                             ; A-Z: call the word. The return address (the IP after the letter) goes on
00C2                             ; the return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
00C2   C5           UPPER:    PUSH   BC   ; the return address, for rpushn
00C3   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; park TOS
00C4   87                     ADD   A,A   
00C5   6F                     LD   L,A   
00C6   26 82                  LD   H,LETPAGE   ; HL -> cell
00C8   4E                     LD   C,(HL)   
00C9   2C                     INC   L   
00CA   46                     LD   B,(HL)   ; IP = the word's body
00CB   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; TOS back, and fall into rpushn
00CC                             ; rpushn: move the top cell of the data stack (in memory) to the return
00CC                             ; stack, then next. Everything that pushes the return stack ends here.
00CC                             ; 
00CC                             ; The break key is looked at here, so at every word call and loop-back (and
00CC                             ; block entry and "{"), but only one time in 256: B', which nothing else
00CC                             ; uses, counts them. Reading the keyboard can be slow (it is a BDOS call
00CC                             ; under CP/M), and this way it costs a loop four bytes and 14 T-states.
00CC                             ; (DEC B, not DJNZ: its zero flag lasts through the EXX, so one EXX serves
00CC                             ; both ways out.)
